   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "נָשָׂא אִשָּׁה כּוּ׳. הָא גּוּפַהּ קַשְׁיָא:",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught that if «one married a woman» in Eretz Yisrael and divorced her in Cappadocia, he must pay her the marriage contract in the currency of Eretz Yisrael. The same is true if he married her in Cappadocia and divorced her in Eretz Yisrael. The Gemara asks: «This matter itself is difficult,» i.e., there is an internal contradiction in the rulings provided by the mishna."
  }
